WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.176
Have you ever searched online for football boots, and then seen adverts for boots everywhere the next day? That is not luck. The advert was chosen for you.

00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:23.291
This is targeted online advertising. It shows adverts only to people likely to be interested, based on their searches, purchases or profile.

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:40.559
Step one: name the digital tool. Besides targeted adverts, there is social media; viral adverts, which people share quickly with each other; e-newsletters, which a business sends electronically to its customers; and the business's own website.

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:53.279
Step two: say what makes it useful. Digital promotion can reach people worldwide, at any time, often more cheaply than traditional methods, and it can be precisely targeted.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:01:01.485
Step three: link the tool to sales, repeat purchases or loyalty. So the chain is: the tool, why it is useful, then the result.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:16.004
Step four: social media has two sides. Good reviews spread quickly and attract customers. But bad or untrue reviews can drive customers away, and not everyone uses social media.

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:30.776
Here is a real question from Paper two R in June 2019. Explain one advantage for a business of using targeted advertising online. It is worth three marks.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:41.746
Mark one is the advantage. The adverts reach the people most likely to be interested, such as those who recently searched for similar products.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:53.796
Mark two explains why that matters. Fewer adverts are wasted on people who would never buy, so the business gets better value than with many traditional methods.

00:01:54.350 --> 00:02:00.847
Mark three is the result. More of the people who see the advert go on to buy, so sales increase.

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:11.866
Mistake one: saying online advertising is good with no reason. Give the reason, such as targeting or low cost.

00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:16.770
Mistake two: defining an e-newsletter when the question asks for a benefit.

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:32.474
Now you try. A small cake shop has two thousand followers on social media. Explain one disadvantage of social media for the shop. Pause here and work it out.

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:48.754
One unhappy customer may post a bad review, or even an untrue one. Many of the two thousand followers could see it quickly. Some may then buy their cakes elsewhere, so the shop's sales fall.

00:02:49.350 --> 00:02:58.167
That is the method for this type: name the digital tool, say why it is useful or risky, then link it to sales. Now try the practice questions.
